---
---Whether the recipe should be included in the recycling recipes automatically generated by the quality mod.
---
---This property is not read by the game engine itself, but the quality mod's recycling.lua file. This means it is discarded by the game engine after loading finishes.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/RecipePrototype.html%23auto_recycle#auto_recycle)
---@field auto_recycle? boolean
---@
---
---When set to `true`, player can set quality of this recipe to craft. If set to `false` then this recipe can only be crafted at normal quality.
---
---Defaults to `true` if recipe is a parameter, or has at least one item ingredient that does not have any of [quality\_min](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemIngredientPrototype.html%23quality_min#quality_min), [quality\_max](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemIngredientPrototype.html%23quality_max#quality_max),  or [quality\_change](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/types/ItemIngredientPrototype.html%23quality_change#quality_change) set.
---
---This property also influences the automatic [Furnace Recipe Selection](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/furnace-recipe-selection.html).
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/RecipePrototype.html%23can_set_quality#can_set_quality)
---@field can_set_quality? boolean
---@
---
---The [categories](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/RecipeCategory.html) of this recipe. Controls which machines can craft this recipe.
---
---The built-in categories can be found [here](https://wiki.factorio.com/Data.raw#recipe-category). The base `"crafting"` category can not contain recipes with fluid ingredients or products.
---
---The array must contain at least one category, it cannot be empty.
---
---[View Documentation](https://lua-api.factorio.com/latest/prototypes/RecipePrototype.html%23categories#categories)
---@field categories? (RecipeCategoryID)[]
---@
